energy-pie-92cd1760.symmetry_origin:
This equation originates from the Friedmann equations, which are derived from Einstein's field equations of General Relativity applied to a homogeneous and isotropic universe described by the FLRW metric. The spatial flatness condition (

$\Omega_{tot} = 1$

) signifies a specific symmetry in the spatial geometry, akin to Euclidean geometry on a large scale. It is a consequence of how mass-energy influences spacetime curvature, as dictated by the equivalence principle and the tensor nature of gravity.

